# Proofestra development workflow

Use the user's current requested development roles: **GPT Sol** for planner and
designer, **Opus 5.5** for reviewer and advisor, and **Sonet 5.5** (the user's
exact spelling) for worker. Before assigning substantive new implementation,
inspect Cursor's actual available model names and record the selected model for
each role. If the UI identifies **Sonnet 5.5** as the intended worker, record that
verified mapping explicitly. Do not silently substitute another model or claim
these models ran merely because this instruction exists. An unavailable model or
unavailable model picker is a specific blocker for that role; continue independent
verification and preparation, then report the blocker. Never create a new grant,
subscription, paid API call or spending authorization to satisfy this rule.

For every material change, use a plan, worker implementation and independent
review/advice in those roles. Preserve existing work and follow AGENTS.md and
docs/development-policy.md. Rules are persistent instructions; they do not prove
model availability or automatically enforce the selected model in Cursor.

Run npm run test:coverage before declaring a release ready. Statements, branches,
functions and lines must each be at least 90% across all production src/**/*.ts
and src/**/*.tsx, including unimported files. Do not lower thresholds, broadly
exclude code, add coverage-ignore directives, or write trivial invocation tests
to make the gate pass. Test meaningful user outcomes, failure and cancellation
paths. Report actual percentages and any failing gate; a passing test count is
not a coverage percentage. Mock and intercepted-wire tests are not live tests.

